<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sigismund III Vasa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1566">1566</a>–<a href="/years/1632">1632</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-vasa">House of Vasa</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sigismund III Vasa was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and grand duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> from 1587 to 1632, and king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> from 1592 until he was deposed in 1599. A zealous Catholic, he moved the royal residence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a> and fought long wars with Sweden, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>; during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/time-of-troubles">Time of Troubles</a> his forces occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sigismund-iii-vasa.jpg" alt="Sigismund III Vasa" width="320" height="544" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pieter Soutman · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soutman_Sigismund_III_Vasa_in_coronation_robes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…Żółkiewski defeated a larger Russian and Swedish force at the Battle of Klushino and Polish troops occupied Moscow, where a group of boyars elected <b>Sigismund III</b>’s son Władysław, the future Władysław IV, as Tsar, an overreach that proved unsustainable but illustrated the Commonwealth’s offensive reach at its peak.</blockquote><a href="/empire/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In the final phase of Sweden's civil war, supporters of the deposed King <b>Sigismund III Vasa</b> were publicly executed at Turku (Åbo) in Finland.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-10">10 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Sigismund III Vasa</b>, king of Poland and grand duke of Lithuania since 1587, succeeded his father John III as King of Sweden.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-17">17 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote>In the Senate Hall of the Royal Castle in Warsaw, Shuisky, deposed in Russia, and his retinue paid homage to King <b>Sigismund III Vasa</b> of Poland and the teenage Prince Władysław.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-29">29 October in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gripsholm-castle">Gripsholm Castle</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/sweden">Sweden</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=59.26,17.22&amp;year=1608" aria-label="Gripsholm Castle on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4913 172 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Sigismund III Vasa"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5363 442h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5363 442h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=59.26,17.22&amp;year=1608">What was here in 1608? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
